{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"aquila-g0207","name":"Aquila","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"claudius-g2804g","name":"Claudius","kind":"person","brief":"Roman Emperor","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"priscilla-g4252","name":"Priscilla","kind":"person","brief":"Christian teacher","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"javan-h3120g","name":"Javan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Japheth","count":1,"firstVerse":4}],"places":[{"id":"athens-g0116","name":"Athens","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"corinth-g2882","name":"Corinth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"italy-g2482","name":"Italy","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"pontus-g4195","name":"Pontus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":194},{"base":"G5563","lemma":"χωρίζω","tr":"chōrizō","gloss":"to separate","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"G2804","lemma":"Κλαύδιος","tr":"Klaudios","gloss":"Claudius","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4252","lemma":"Πρίσκιλλα","tr":"Priskilla","gloss":"Priscilla","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5078","lemma":"τέχνη","tr":"technē","gloss":"skill","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0116","lemma":"Ἀθῆναι","tr":"Athēnai","gloss":"Athens","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2482","lemma":"Ἰταλία","tr":"Italia","gloss":"Italy","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0207","lemma":"Ἀκύλας","tr":"Akulas","gloss":"Aquila","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G2882","lemma":"Κόρινθος","tr":"Korinthos","gloss":"Corinth","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G2064","lemma":"ἔρχομαι","tr":"erchomai","gloss":"to come","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":631}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Greet Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus,","from":2},{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"who have risked their lives for me. Not only I but all the churches of the Gentiles are grateful to them.","from":2},{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.","from":2},{"book":"1TH","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Surely you recall, brothers, our labor and toil. We worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to anyone while we proclaimed to you the gospel of God.","from":3},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Greet Prisca and Aquila, as well as the household of Onesiphorus.","from":2},{"book":"1CO","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"We work hard with our own hands. When we are vilified, we bless; when we are persecuted, we endure it;","from":3},{"book":"ACT","chapter":11,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"One of them named Agabus stood up and predicted through the Spirit that a great famine would sweep across the whole world. (This happened under Claudius.)","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. When Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him aside and explained to him the way of God more accurately.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"5-8":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"silas-g4609","name":"Silas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"justus-g2459g","name":"Justus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"crispus-g2921","name":"Crispus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"corinth-g2882","name":"Corinth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"G3614","lemma":"οἰκία","tr":"oikia","gloss":"home","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":93},{"base":"G4100","lemma":"πιστεύω","tr":"pisteuō","gloss":"to trust (in)","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":237},{"base":"G2881","lemma":"Κορίνθιος","tr":"Korinthios","gloss":"Corinthian","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2921","lemma":"Κρίσπος","tr":"Krispos","gloss":"Crispus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2459","lemma":"Ἰοῦστος","tr":"Ioustos","gloss":"Justus","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1621","lemma":"ἐκτινάσσω","tr":"ektinassō","gloss":"to shake out","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0498","lemma":"ἀντιτάσσω","tr":"antitassō","gloss":"to resist","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G0575","lemma":"ἀπό","tr":"apo","gloss":"away from","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":644},{"base":"G0752","lemma":"ἀρχισυνάγωγος","tr":"archisunagōgos","gloss":"synagogue leader","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G4576","lemma":"σέβομαι","tr":"sebomai","gloss":"be devout","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZK","chapter":33,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"Then if anyone hears the sound of the horn but fails to heed the warning, and the sword comes and takes him away, his blood will be on his own head.","from":6},{"book":"2SA","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"For David had said to the Amalekite, “Your blood be on your own head because your own mouth has testified against you, saying, ‘I killed the LORDʼs anointed.’”","from":6},{"book":"EZK","chapter":33,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"If I say to the wicked, ‘O wicked man, you will surely die,’ but you do not speak out to dissuade him from his way, then that wicked man will die in his iniquity, yet I will hold you accountable for his blood.","from":6},{"book":"EZK","chapter":33,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"But if you warn the wicked man to turn from his way, and he does not turn from it, he will die in his iniquity, but you will have saved your life.","from":6},{"book":"EZK","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"He engages in usury and takes excess interest. Will this son live? He will not! Since he has committed all these abominations, he will surely die; his blood will be on his own head.","from":6},{"book":"NEH","chapter":5,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"I also shook out the folds of my robe and said, “May God likewise shake out of his house and possession every man who does not keep this promise. May such a man be shaken out and have nothing!” The whole assembly said, “Amen,” and they praised the LORD. And the people did as they had promised.","from":6},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So they shook the dust off their feet in protest against them and went to Iconium.","from":6},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Among those listening was a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, who was a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paulʼs message.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2}]},"9-11":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G1360","lemma":"διότι","tr":"dioti","gloss":"because","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"G2559","lemma":"κακόω","tr":"kakoō","gloss":"to harm","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G4623","lemma":"σιωπάω","tr":"siōpaō","gloss":"be quiet","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G3705","lemma":"ὅραμα","tr":"horama","gloss":"vision","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"G1803","lemma":"ἕξ","tr":"hex","gloss":"six","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G1763","lemma":"ἐνιαυτός","tr":"eniautos","gloss":"year","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G3376","lemma":"μήν","tr":"mēn","gloss":"month","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G3361","lemma":"μή","tr":"mē","gloss":"not","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":1068},{"base":"G2007","lemma":"ἐπιτίθημι","tr":"epitithēmi","gloss":"to put","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":38},{"base":"G2523","lemma":"καθίζω","tr":"kathizō","gloss":"to seat","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":44}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CO","chapter":12,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.","from":10},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Now go! I will help you as you speak, and I will teach you what to say.”","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":41,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Do not fear, for I am with you; do not be afraid, for I am your God. I will strengthen you; I will surely help you; I will uphold you with My righteous right hand.","from":10},{"book":"MAT","chapter":28,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"and teaching them to obey all that I have commanded you. And surely I am with you always, even to the end of the age.”","from":10},{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The following night the Lord stood near Paul and said, “Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so also you must testify in Rome.”","from":9},{"book":"EZK","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"But you, son of man, do not be afraid of them or their words. Do not be afraid, though briers and thorns surround you, and you dwell among scorpions. Do not be afraid of their words or dismayed by their presence, though they are a rebellious house.","from":9},{"book":"EZK","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"And you, son of man, listen to what I tell you. Do not be rebellious like that rebellious house. Open your mouth and eat what I give you.”","from":9},{"book":"JHN","chapter":10,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I have other sheep that are not of this fold. I must bring them in as well, and they will listen to My voice. Then there will be one flock and one shepherd.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-17":{"people":[{"id":"gallio-g1058","name":"Gallio","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"sosthenes-g4988","name":"Sosthenes","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"places":[{"id":"achaia-g0882","name":"Achaia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"words":[{"base":"G1058","lemma":"Γαλλίων","tr":"Galliōn","gloss":"Gallio","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"G0968","lemma":"βῆμα","tr":"bēma","gloss":"judgement seat","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":12},{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":194},{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":158},{"base":"G3551","lemma":"νόμος","tr":"nomos","gloss":"law","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":193},{"base":"G3056","lemma":"λόγος","tr":"logos","gloss":"word","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":329},{"base":"G4988","lemma":"Σωσθένης","tr":"Sōsthenēs","gloss":"Sosthenes","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0092","lemma":"ἀδίκημα","tr":"adikēma","gloss":"crime","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2596","lemma":"κατά","tr":"kata","gloss":"according to","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":472},{"base":"G1487","lemma":"εἰ","tr":"ei","gloss":"if","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":508}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.","from":15},{"book":"ACT","chapter":25,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They only had some contentions with him regarding their own religion and a certain Jesus who had died, but whom Paul affirmed to be alive.","from":15},{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":76,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Even the wrath of man shall praise You; with the survivors of wrath You will clothe Yourself.","from":16},{"book":"AMO","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You drink wine by the bowlful and anoint yourselves with the finest oils, but you fail to grieve over the ruin of Joseph.","from":17},{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“I have sinned by betraying innocent blood,” he said. “What is that to us?” they replied. “You bear the responsibility.”","from":15},{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"While Pilate was sitting on the judgment seat, his wife sent him this message: “Have nothing to do with that innocent man, for I have suffered terribly in a dream today because of Him.”","from":12},{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Pilate saw that he was accomplishing nothing, but that instead a riot was breaking out, he took water and washed his hands before the crowd. “I am innocent of this manʼs blood,” he said. “You bear the responsibility.”","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"18-23":{"people":[{"id":"aquila-g0207","name":"Aquila","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"priscilla-g4252","name":"Priscilla","kind":"person","brief":"Christian teacher","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"cenchreae-g2747","name":"Cenchreae","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"ephesus-g2181","name":"Ephesus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"antioch-g0490g","name":"Antioch","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"caesarea-g2542h","name":"Caesarea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"galatia-g1053","name":"Galatia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"phrygia-g5435","name":"Phrygia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"words":[{"base":"G0657","lemma":"ἀποτάσσω","tr":"apotassō","gloss":"to leave","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"G2181","lemma":"Ἔφεσος","tr":"ephesos","gloss":"Ephesus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"G5550","lemma":"χρόνος","tr":"chronos","gloss":"time","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":54},{"base":"G1054","lemma":"Γαλατικός","tr":"Galatikos","gloss":"Galatia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2747","lemma":"Κεγχρεαί","tr":"Kegchreai","gloss":"Cenchreae","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1602","lemma":"ἐκπλέω","tr":"ekpleō","gloss":"to sail out","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2171","lemma":"εὐχή","tr":"euchē","gloss":"a vow","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4252","lemma":"Πρίσκιλλα","tr":"Priskilla","gloss":"Priscilla","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5435","lemma":"Φρυγία","tr":"Phrugia","gloss":"Phrygia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0344","lemma":"ἀνακάμπτω","tr":"anakamptō","gloss":"to return","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":21,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Take these men, purify yourself along with them, and pay their expenses so they can have their heads shaved. Then everyone will know that there is no truth to these rumors about you, but that you also live in obedience to the law.","from":18},{"book":"NUM","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, the Nazirite is to shave his consecrated head, take the hair, and put it on the fire under the peace offering.","from":18},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"strengthening the souls of the disciples and encouraging them to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” they said.","from":23},{"book":"1CO","chapter":4,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing, and then I will find out not only what these arrogant people are saying, but what power they have.","from":21},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"After the Holy Spirit had prevented them from speaking the word in the province of Asia, they traveled through the region of Phrygia and Galatia.","from":23},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"in my prayers at all times, asking that now at last by Godʼs will I may succeed in coming to you.","from":21},{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"so that by Godʼs will I may come to you with joy and together with you be refreshed.","from":21},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, To the saints in Ephesus, the faithful in Christ Jesus:","from":19}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4}]},"24-28":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"apollos-g0625","name":"Apollos","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"john-g2491g","name":"John","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"aquila-g0207","name":"Aquila","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"priscilla-g4252","name":"Priscilla","kind":"person","brief":"Christian teacher","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":28}],"places":[{"id":"alexandria-g0222","name":"Alexandria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"ephesus-g2181","name":"Ephesus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"achaia-g0882","name":"Achaia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"words":[{"base":"G1124","lemma":"γραφή","tr":"graphē","gloss":"a writing","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":50},{"base":"G3598","lemma":"ὁδός","tr":"hodos","gloss":"road","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":101},{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":194},{"base":"G0221","lemma":"Ἀλεξανδρεύς","tr":"Alexandreus","gloss":"Alexandrian","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2159","lemma":"εὐτόνως","tr":"eutonōs","gloss":"vehemently","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2204","lemma":"ζέω","tr":"zeō","gloss":"be fervent","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G4252","lemma":"Πρίσκιλλα","tr":"Priskilla","gloss":"Priscilla","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0197","lemma":"ἀκριβέστερον","tr":"akribesteron","gloss":"stricter","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G1219","lemma":"δημόσιος","tr":"dēmosios","gloss":"public","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G1620","lemma":"ἐκτίθημι","tr":"ektithēmi","gloss":"to explain","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.","from":28},{"book":"1CO","chapter":3,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"What then is Apollos? And what is Paul? They are servants through whom you believed, as the Lord has assigned to each his role.","from":24},{"book":"1CO","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow.","from":24},{"book":"1CO","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Brothers, I have applied these things to myself and Apollos for your benefit, so that you may learn from us not to go beyond what is written. Then you will not take pride in one man over another.","from":24},{"book":"TIT","chapter":3,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Do your best to equip Zenas the lawyer and Apollos, so that they will have everything they need.","from":24},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Into what, then, were you baptized?” Paul asked. “The baptism of John,” they replied.","from":25},{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"What I mean is this: Individuals among you are saying, “I follow Paul,” “I follow Apollos,” “I follow Cephas,” or “I follow Christ.”","from":24},{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now about our brother Apollos: I strongly urged him to go to you with the brothers. He was not at all inclined to go now, but he will go when he has the opportunity.","from":24}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":5},{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jesus-family","title":"Jesus and His Family Circle","people":2}]}}